  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "$\\int ({sech}^{2}\u2061z+\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z\\operatorname{coth}\u2061z)\\,\\text{d}z=$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z)=-\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z\\operatorname{coth}\u2061z & \\,\u21d2\\,\\int \\operatorname{csch}\u2061z\\operatorname{coth}\u2061z\\,\\text{d}z=-\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}z}(\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061z)={sech}^{2}\u2061z & \\,\u21d2\\,\\int {sech}^{2}\u2061z\\,\\text{d}z=\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061z+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sech}^{2}\u2061z+\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z\\operatorname{coth}\u2061z)\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int {sech}^{2}\u2061z\\,\\text{d}z+\\int \\operatorname{csch}\u2061z\\operatorname{coth}\u2061z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061z-\\operatorname{csch}\u2061z+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
